-+## Changed
-+
-+- Replaced Rust approve's stacking refusal with the TypeScript-compatible stacked approval: the selection follows declared `depends_on` entries, the change's own `.run/stacked-on` overlap lines, capability overlaps, the chain-tip closure rule, and approved/archived hashes from branches, stacked copies and the checkout.
-+- Added the stacked approval write path: it replaces `<stacked>`, copies the checkout change folder, writes `.run/approved`, `.run/approver` and `.run/stacked-on` with no trailing newline on the last line, removes the checkout copy unless HEAD holds it, and writes no branch, worktree, commit, `.run/base`, event or tree record line.
-+- Moved the rejected branch rename into the refusal phase so it runs once before either a stacked or worktree approval writes.
-+- Rewrote `approve_stacking.rs` for every row of "What a stacked approval waits for", added a checkout-marker regression case, and added `approve_stacked.rs` for every golden row plus "Stacked folder replaced".
-+- Copied the stacked goldens unchanged into `crates/features/approve/tests/fixtures/stacked-golden`.
-+
-+## Deviated
-+
-+- Added one extra test beyond the scenario rows, `checkout_marker_awaits`, to keep the checkout approval-marker read covered after removing the old refusal test.
-+
-+## Outside scope
-+
-+- The proposal verify `sh scripts/verify-rust.sh` fails in the unrelated corpus test `crates/core/tests/event_corpus.rs` on `openspec/changes/archive/340-overlap-wait-survives-reapproval/.run/events/1.jsonl:87` with `invalid data for event type \`dead\``. The task verify passes, and that archived event file is outside this task's scope.
