+- Replaced Rust approve's stacking refusal with the TypeScript-compatible
+  stacked approval: the selection follows declared `depends_on` entries, the
+  change's own `.run/stacked-on` overlap lines, capability overlaps, the
+  chain-tip closure rule, and approved/archived hashes from branches, stacked
+  copies and the checkout.
+- Added the stacked approval write path: it replaces `<stacked>`, copies the
+  checkout change folder, writes `.run/approved`, `.run/approver` and
+  `.run/stacked-on` with no trailing newline on the last line, removes the
+  checkout copy unless HEAD holds it, and writes no branch, worktree, commit,
+  `.run/base`, event or tree record line.
+- Moved the rejected branch rename into the refusal phase so it runs once
+  before either a stacked or worktree approval writes.
+- Rewrote `approve_stacking.rs` for every row of "What a stacked approval
+  waits for", kept a checkout-marker regression case, and added
+  `approve_stacked.rs` for every golden row plus "Stacked folder replaced".
